q("DRAG", "Induced drag is caused by:", ["Wing tip vortices and downwash", "Skin friction in the boundary layer", "Junctions between aircraft parts", "Shock waves on the upper surface"], "La différence de pression crée des tourbillons qui inclinent la portance vers l'arrière.")
q("DRAG", "Interference drag is generated:", ["At junctions such as wing to fuselage", "At the wing tips by vortices", "In the boundary layer only", "Only at transonic speeds"], "Deux écoulements se gênent aux jonctions. Réduite par des carénages (fairings).")
q("DRAG", "Interference drag can be reduced by:", ["Fairings at the junctions", "Increasing the aspect ratio", "Using winglets", "Increasing the wing loading"], "")
q("DRAG", "Parasite drag includes:", ["Skin friction, form and interference drag", "Induced drag and interference drag", "Wave drag and induced drag", "Form drag and induced drag"], "")
q("DRAG", "Total drag is minimum where:", ["Induced drag equals parasite drag", "Induced drag is lower than parasite", "Parasite drag is at its minimum", "Lift is equal to aircraft weight"], "Au point Vmd, creux de la courbe en U.")
q("DRAG", "The speed for minimum drag (VMD) also gives:", ["The maximum lift/drag ratio", "The maximum rate of climb", "The minimum stall speed", "The maximum true airspeed"], "Finesse maximale = traînée minimale à poids constant.")
q("DRAG", "Flying slower than VMD is called:", ["The second regime (back side of the drag curve)", "The first regime (front side of the drag curve)", "The transonic regime", "The ground effect regime"], "")
q("DRAG", "On the back side of the drag curve, if speed decreases:", ["Drag increases, so speed keeps decreasing", "Drag decreases, so speed recovers by itself", "Drag stays constant", "The aircraft automatically climbs"], "Second régime : instable en vitesse. Il faut plus de puissance pour voler plus lentement.")
q("DRAG", "In the first regime (above VMD), speed stability is:", ["Positive: the aircraft returns to its speed", "Negative: the speed keeps decreasing", "Neutral: the speed never changes", "Only positive with flaps extended"], "Si la vitesse baisse, la traînée baisse et l'avion réaccélère.")
q("DRAG", "If aircraft mass increases, the total drag curve:", ["Moves up and VMD increases", "Moves down and VMD decreases", "Does not change", "Moves up and VMD decreases"], "Plus de masse, plus de portance, donc plus de traînée induite.")
q("DRAG", "Induced drag can be reduced by:", ["High aspect ratio and winglets", "Low aspect ratio and wing fences", "Higher wing loading and flaps", "Thicker airfoil and rough surface"], "Cxi = CL² / (π λ).")
q("DRAG", "Aspect ratio is:", ["Wing span squared divided by wing area", "Wing area divided by wing span", "Tip chord divided by root chord", "Wing span divided by fuselage length"], "λ = b² / S.")
q("DRAG", "At low speed in level flight, which drag is dominant?", ["Induced drag", "Parasite drag", "Wave drag", "Interference drag"], "")
q("DRAG", "Skin friction drag is higher with:", ["A turbulent boundary layer", "A laminar boundary layer", "A smaller wetted area", "A lower airspeed"], "La couche turbulente frotte plus, mais décolle moins vite.")

